{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_061443f6fbf1666e09cfda538d1a84a9cb2c5d20e278ae97e2d59bd1f3f927b0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Coding tests for simulated students run in three steps via dedicated scripts: pre-test, student code generation, and coding-test metrics."},{"claim_ids":["clm_236a6b104b0c2ef259fc43c18298775faab59781d56b9d245b18c7f806c0381b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A trained verifier checkpoint (Verifier-7B) is released for download on Hugging Face."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4231913bce16f44d08ad5cc9381a99f89a95b89b1301861908eaf115025b112d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Although coding tutoring is the example scenario, the authors state the method extends to other task-tutoring settings where content must adapt to users' varying background knowledge."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5054a540a2958f92b04001626ddc40a1fc57bb37f1289c6648a91effc7d96024"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The work introduces DICT, an evaluation protocol combining student simulation with coding tests to assess tutoring performance."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5102e68f914185e003c7566a3af62d517a4211714ce5c1045ccf2964494bde09"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Released simulated dialogues are stored as JSON records containing a namespace field and a conversation list with alternating tutor and student entries."},{"claim_ids":["clm_55ec0cb49ccb596a6e6c9cf7fa93193b7b66f15ae139deafa884b724b3e4f767"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Users must configure their own Azure API key, data path, and model path based on files under scripts/run/ before use."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5c83a36032a87160a57ebe51c5a24faf497ed9c07bf55b8e85838d2b6f5e9287"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README reports that simulated students at different levels show distinct task-completion abilities, and presents DICT as a scalable, cost-effective proxy for human evaluation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_663a54f10b3b7e9a4e34c4a89a38bb19dab78ea3cfe61b0ff66ee623d748a05d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README reports that the Traver workflow with the trained verifier exhibits inference-time scaling for coding tutoring."},{"claim_ids":["clm_74863043154dcb90579b31103e2bdf12b9bef30309758e415a85a9b7f0b8033d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is installed via a Python 3.10 conda environment followed by pip install -r requirements.txt."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7883b608de9ae388fabb8bca6aaaa8f0ef0ed30cf7baa5a35b8f5fe38d42f0d8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project proposes Traver (Trace-and-Verify), an agent workflow that incorporates knowledge tracing and turn-by-turn verification for coding tutoring."},{"claim_ids":["clm_862fd44c5f96d4486ac3fe20a6d718bb7990aa8ea2fe48d1beeae3b861d3e86d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Setup requires downloading EvoCodeBench-2403 and building its execution environment per that project's instructions, which the README notes can take a few hours."},{"claim_ids":["clm_88b02c1fc04f4f981b1da4b087de3f0d2a836d541e55d4e3b48d2e9e04f13ca8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The work was accepted to ACL Findings 2025 and released on arXiv (2502.13311) in February 2025."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b5d95599ba410e83664262048d3b919616e7a76222e8d7f37e4472ec8ccb4072"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Evaluation scripts cover pre-test performance, tutoring outcome (TOR) computed from pre- and post-test directories, and tutoring outcome curves (TOC)."}],"claim_ids":["clm_061443f6fbf1666e09cfda538d1a84a9cb2c5d20e278ae97e2d59bd1f3f927b0","clm_236a6b104b0c2ef259fc43c18298775faab59781d56b9d245b18c7f806c0381b","clm_4231913bce16f44d08ad5cc9381a99f89a95b89b1301861908eaf115025b112d","clm_5054a540a2958f92b04001626ddc40a1fc57bb37f1289c6648a91effc7d96024","clm_5102e68f914185e003c7566a3af62d517a4211714ce5c1045ccf2964494bde09","clm_55ec0cb49ccb596a6e6c9cf7fa93193b7b66f15ae139deafa884b724b3e4f767","clm_5c83a36032a87160a57ebe51c5a24faf497ed9c07bf55b8e85838d2b6f5e9287","clm_663a54f10b3b7e9a4e34c4a89a38bb19dab78ea3cfe61b0ff66ee623d748a05d","clm_74863043154dcb90579b31103e2bd